,"severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bc66efbf5c032093cfa229760fb132a1c7f4ae60.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.bc66efbf5c032093cfa229760fb132a1c7f4ae60.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 23 at 10:35AM MDT until October 23 at 12:45PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Western Conejos County in south central Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1245 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of the Conejos River, area creeks, streams, and\nother low-lying and flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\nStreams continue to rise due to excess runoff from earlier\nrainfall.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1031 AM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain. Flooding is already occurring in the warned area.\nBetween 1 and 3 inches of rain have fallen. Significant impacts\nto homes along the Conejos River and water over Highway 17 have\nbeen reported.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nCumbres Pass, Platoro, Mogote.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T12:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Conejos, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ce4f4948f1c76273375a3301a6ef2c557f12304b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.ce4f4948f1c76273375a3301a6ef2c557f12304b.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued October 23 at 7:40AM MDT until October 23 at 6:00PM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n\n* WHEN...Until 6 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Light to moderate rain showers will continue across the southwest\nmountains through the morning, with scattered showers and\npossible thunderstorms, developing across the region through the\nafternoon. Rain, locally heavy associated with the afternoon\nshowers and thunderstorms, will exacerbate ongoing flooding\nissues across the eastern San Juan mountains and Upper Rio Grande\nvalley.\n- The eastern San Juan Mountains and Upper Rio Grande Valley.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Upper Rio Grande Valley/Eastern San Juan Mountains Below 10000 Ft; Eastern San Juan Mountains Above 10000 Ft","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f57ec630e3f51d7902083d7b452bfaf33433f7ba.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f57ec630e3f51d7902083d7b452bfaf33433f7ba.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T17:09:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 231709 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1109 AM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flood Watch remains in effect through this afternoon for the eastern San Juan mountains and the Upper Rio Grande Valley, with stream/river flooding and rock/mud slides possible. - Rainfall starting to diminish across the higher terrain through this morning, then ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T17:58:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 231758 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1158 AM MDT Fri Oct 23 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-241800- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=HWO&format=CI"},"fwf":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T06:45:00+00:00","snippet